      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arcsine",
      "problem": "$\\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-6\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
