      "math_academy_id": "e-386",
      "knowledge_point_id": "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arcsine",
      "problem": "Calculate the indefinite integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x = \\arcsin (x) + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
