      "knowledge_point_id": "d7256d2e-7105-5a4e-8d0a-5e00dfc1e311",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arctangent",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
